    "Staging Cloudflare Pages preview returns x-robots-tag: noindex (re-verified 2026-09-29), so the Lighthouse is-crawlable audit fails on all 6 URLs and deflates the SEO category to 69. SEO is recorded but EXCLUDED from all verdicts this run. Status: inconclusive - staging noindex artifact, re-audit after apex cutover.",
    "APEX IS LIVE BUT CUTOVER NOT RECORDED: https://tdiusa.com/ and https://www.tdiusa.com/ both return HTTP 200 serving the new Astro build (identical _astro asset hashes to staging, no noindex). Last month tdiusa.com 302-redirected to the old Scorpion site. The client record has no apex_cutover.completed_at, so per methodology this run still audited staging. A supplementary desktop Lighthouse run on https://www.tdiusa.com/ scored performance 99, accessibility 92, best practices 100, SEO 100 (recorded under supplementary_apex_check, not counted in verdicts).",
    "Canonicals now point to https://www.tdiusa.com/... (last month: https://tdiusa.com/...). The non-www apex serves 200 rather than 301 to www, and robots.txt declares Sitemap: https://tdiusa.com/sitemap-index.xml (non-www). Host is inconsistent across canonical, sitemap, and client record domain.",
    "DataForSEO instant_pages returned has_micromarkup=false again; JSON-LD is present and parses on every page (types listed per URL under onpage_summary.jsonld_types_verified). Treated as a DataForSEO false negative.",
    "Client record status is \"onboarding\", not \"active\". Audit proceeded on build_status=pushed_main, consistent with the 2026-08-28 run and the scheduler System 3 gate.",
    "Lighthouse 13.4.0 agentic-browsing category recorded per URL as agentic_browsing_score but excluded from verdicts.",
    "on_page_lighthouse / on_page_instant_pages MCP tools are absent from this MCP build; endpoints called directly via /v3/on_page/lighthouse/live/json (for_mobile=false) and /v3/on_page/instant_pages. Full Lighthouse JSON was written to disk and parsed there.",
    "Word counts come from DataForSEO plain_text_word_count; the 2026-08-28 run reported different absolute counts for the same pages, so month-over-month word count changes are not meaningful."
